BidsTest
├── When the payment is zero
│   └── It should revert.
├── When the cutoff is reached
│   └── It should reject new bids and cancellation.
├── When there is no inventory
│   └── It should revert.
├── When a bidder increases their offer
│   └── It should charge only the top up and preserve total escrow.
├── When equal bids exist
│   └── It should prefer the earlier accepted amount.
├── When a losing bidder cancels
│   └── It should refund only their funds and preserve the leader.
├── When the leader cancels before cutoff
│   └── It should promote the next highest bid.
├── When the refund recipient rejects ETH
│   └── It should revert without removing the bid.
├── When a bid rolls into the next day
│   └── It should remain funded without charging again.
├── When the winner bids again
│   └── It should create a separate funded offer.
├── When a refund recipient attempts reentrancy
│   └── It should block duplicate withdrawal.
├── When the recipient is invalid
│   └── It should revert.
├── When the bidder has no offer
│   └── It should revert.
├── When middle and tail bidders at an equal price cancel
│   └── It should preserve the remaining queue and lower price bids.
├── When the head of an equal price queue wins
│   └── It should roll the remaining bidders forward in their original order.
├── When an emptied price level is reused
│   └── It should restore ordering without retaining stale bidders.
└── When a top up joins an occupied price level
    └── It should join after the existing equal bids.
